  "review_observations": [
    "GetCameraState reads currentState identity once, returns -1 on null/unknown, and does not dereference a TESCameraState. It compares against cameraStates raw pointers.",
    "Metadata and query version are packed 0x02000000; PSC rejects lower versions before acquiring controls or invoking new API 2 methods. Generation is rechecked after new version/API calls.",
    "Acti and Session camera reads use guarded own binding; final Acti/Session disassembly rejects both Camera.GetCameraState and Game.GetCameraState wrappers.",
    "Cleanup can restore owned controls with a missing DLL without calling new native getters. EndSight retains the older >=1 gate because it exists in API 1.",
    "All Session accesses are mutex-protected; key handle acquisition precedes the Session mutex, and VM array allocation/packing follows its release.",
    "Seven RegisterFunction calls use callableFromTasklets=true; custom CaptureAim is explicitly flagged after binding. Scene updates remain in FirstPersonState::Update.",
    "The two shot traces execute after session.capture/session.freeze return; they do not hold the Session mutex and are conditional on accepted shot operations. The selected spdlog sink is basic_file_sink_mt.",
    "Official SKSE NoWait precedents cover camera-state identity, a CreateRefHandle user, and float-array-producing native functions. CommonLib still delegates underlying handle/allocation synchronization to engine functions."
  ],
