    }
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Python fixtures execute selected real PSC branches under deterministic callbacks; they are not the Papyrus VM and do not prove scheduling, persistence or event delivery in Skyrim.",
    "Native Core tests exercise portable session/math logic, not hooked camera consumers, native handle management or the running engine.",
    "No game launch, FPS measurement, firing-latency validation, camera visual validation or engine-load validation was performed.",
    "CommonLib source does not expose the relocated handle-manager or VM array-allocation implementations; NoWait assessment is source-based plus official SKSE precedent.",
    "Shot log intervals are diagnostic timings around accepted operations and are not a proof of visual freeze duration or firing responsiveness.",
    "With a missing/old DLL, perspective restoration is conservatively skipped because the new camera getter is unavailable; owned controls still release."
  ]
